Pistachio Lime Bundt Cake
  --Swapna Sachdev
  
Cake:
2 1/2 c ap flour
1 1/2 c sugar
1 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp baking soda
1 c unsalted butter, at room temperature
1 c shelled unsalted pistachios
4 eggs, at room temperature
1/2 tsp pistachio or almond extract
1 c sour cream
1/8 c milk
1/4 tsp salt

Using a food processor, pulse the pistachios 1/2 c at a time until finely ground. Preheat the oven to 350F/180C and liberally butter and flour a 12 c Bundt pan. In a small bowl whisk together the flour, ground pistachios, baking powder, baking soda and salt. Set aside. Beat the butter and sugar on medium speed with an electric mixer for 3-4 min until light and fluffy. Beat in the eggs, one at a time for 4-5 min until they are well combined. Reduce the speed to low and beat in the flour mixture and sour cream/milk alternately, ending with the flour until just incorporated. Add the batter to the prepared pan, leveling out the top with the spatula. Bake for 55-60 min or until a toothpick inserted near the center comes out clean. Cool on a wire rack for 15-20 min; then invert the cake onto the rack to cool completely.


Glaze:
1 1/2 c confectioners’ sugar
juice of 2 limes
1 tbsp light corn syrup
1/3 c chopped pistachios

Whisk together confectioner’s sugar, lime juice, and corn syrup, Adding the lime juice, 1 tsp at a time, to reach desired consistency. Drizzle this icing over the Bundt cake and sprinkle it with chopped pistachios.
